---
/**
 * The CMS entry point.
 *
 * This lives in src/pages/ rather than public/ deliberately. Astro's dev server
 * serves files in public/ by exact path only -- it does not resolve directory
 * indexes -- so public/admin/index.html was reachable at /admin/index.html but
 * 404'd at /admin/ during development, while GitHub Pages served /admin/ fine.
 * That split meant the URL that works in production was broken locally.
 *
 * As a page route it resolves at /admin/ in both environments and still builds
 * to dist/admin/index.html, so the deployed path is unchanged.
 *
 * config.yml stays in public/admin/ -- it is data the CMS fetches at runtime,
 * not a route, and the CMS looks for it next to this page.
 *
 * CACHE BUSTING: GitHub Pages serves config.yml with `cache-control: max-age=600`
 * and Pages headers cannot be changed. So for ten minutes after every deploy the
 * CMS keeps using the old config -- a newly added category or field simply is not
 * there, with no error to explain why. The `cms-config-url` link lets us point
 * Sveltia at a versioned URL that changes on every build, so a deploy always
 * invalidates it. The file itself is ~9 KB, so refetching costs nothing.
 */
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';

// Changes on every build, which is exactly the point.
const configUrl = withBase(`/admin/config.yml?v=${Date.now().toString(36)}`);
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <!-- Keep the admin UI out of search results. -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Portfolio CMS</title>
    <link href={configUrl} type="text/yaml" rel="cms-config-url" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/@sveltia/cms/dist/sveltia-cms.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
